<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκόρ-ισμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a coaxing</i> or <i>endearing name,</i> as Dem. said
			that his nickname <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάταλος</span> was a
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τίτθης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.126
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>a fair name</i> for something base, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράσιτος</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυφάγος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				178.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				219.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεισάχθεια</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρεῶν ἀποκοπή,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.807e
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυγῆς ὑ. καὶ παρακάλυμμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Galb.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>diminutive,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1540.54
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
